en:
So they gave up and went to culinary school to try to recreate that candy on their own.
Talk about obsessed.
But in the end they gave up on that too and just became a regular chef.{p}

"No luck today either..."
The sun had gone down completely, and there were no students left heading home from school.
Sakuma pinned his hopes on tomorrow once again and decided to go home.{p}

He ran like a madman.
When he finally stopped, unable to run another step, the old lady was nowhere to be seen.
Then he opened the hand still clutching the candy tight.{p}

"...My life's been the pits until now.
But that's all gonna change.
Take that, all of you."{p}

The door was locked.
If he ignored her, she'd give up and leave.
Sakuma took a deep breath to calm himself down.{p}

"Gyaaaaaaaaah!"
Sakuma's scream rang through the whole house.
Startled by it, his family went to his room, and...{p}

Katagiri was heading out the school gate, putting up with the pain of her cavities.
Just then, a voice called out to her.
"All by yourself, are you, dearie?"{p}

She turned around, and what do you know, there stood an old lady with a red hood pulled low over her eyes.
It was the Candy Granny.
There hadn't been anyone there a moment ago, but she'd appeared like a puff of smoke.{p}

Right, then you know.
That kind of pain.
Katagiri was hurting like that too.{p}

She seized the girl's hand in her wrinkled one and pressed something into it.
"...Candy?"
When she opened her hand, there was a huge ball of candy, about the size of a golf ball, in a crumpled wrapper.{p}

"Eriko's kind of changed, hasn't she?"
"Seriously. She gives off this really nasty vibe."
What happened to Hara, you ask?{p}

Pretty funny, huh?
And Katagiri had sucked on the exact same candy.
After that, they say, the old lady stopped showing up altogether.{p}

"Whatever, just hurry up and give me the candy.
That's why you showed up in front of me, right?"
That's what he went and said.{p}

"What an impatient child.
Well then, I suppose I'll give you some candy.
But, you know..."{p}

"And here I was, going to warn you.
Well, you can just learn it the hard way, firsthand.
Hee hee hee."{p}

Then he called a guy who'd gotten candy from her before into the restroom.
"Please, trade tongues with me.
I've had it with that candy."{p}

"Now I never have to taste that candy again.
Ahahahaha!"
Sakuma ran off down the hallway, flicking his tongue in and out, all slick with some lukewarm, reeking fluid.{p}

A student who saw him tearing down the hallway toward them was so scared their legs gave out, and they couldn't move.
"Eek, eeeeek☆"
As he went by, Sakuma licked the student's face once, and the student couldn't remember what happened after that; when they came to, they were lying in a bed in the nurse's office.{p}

Because within a month of that moment, Sakuma will come to gouge out your eyeballs.
Not saying it is easy. Not thinking it is the hard part, right?
When you try not to think about it, you end up thinking about it even more.{p}
